I’m applying the stronger experiment: both independent employers must actually pay €5,500, through different routes, while the entrant retains the relationship and unit costs fit the 49% mature design. That keeps the verdict unchanged but makes its decisive assumption genuinely testable. I’m also treating the capacity figures as explicit design hurdles, not observed rates.
