 <p>Year one is paid evidence. Six field jobs require roughly two founder days each plus selling and coordination. It fits beside a job only with booked site days and a partner who absorbs schedule variance. The loss after founder replacement is honest: the test does not replace developer income.</p>
+<p>The mature workload assumes 35 model-only baselines, 15 measured baselines and 60 change reviews. For hygienists, allow three hours per model-only baseline, ten per measured baseline and two per review. That is 375 delivery hours, plus 25 reserve hours, at a €200 hourly hurdle: €80,000.</p>
+<p>For the technician, allow 12 hours per model-only baseline, 28 per measured baseline and five per review. That is 1,140 delivery hours plus 485 paid hours for travel, setup, idle time and training. At a €40 hourly hurdle, 1,625 paid hours cost €65,000. The 15 measured baselines consume 420 technician hours and permit work across multiple days.</p>
+<p>The founder spends five hours per baseline and three per review, or 430 delivery hours. Another 570 cover selling, partner coordination, quality control and exceptions. At a €100 replacement-cost hurdle, 1,000 founder hours produce the €100,000 line. The technician allocation is one full paid year; the founder allocation is about three fifths of that capacity.</p>
