@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@
 <p>Polish and Russian help where the assessment depends on what workers actually do: how they mix, spray, clean, remove protection and respond to a blocked hose. The reader's CEE network can reach subcontracted crews and foreign-owned shops that a national provider may serve awkwardly. Those are working hypotheses from the edge inventory, not evidence that most Dutch spray crews speak these languages.</p>
 <p>The Dutch gate is real twice. First, the employer, RI&amp;E owner and Inspectorate operate in Dutch. A2 is not enough to discover commercial ambiguity or defend a technical report. Second, the Inspectorate expects occupational-hygienist-level expertise. <!-- CHECK: 04-expert-gate --> Its page names a competence level, not a statutory licence or an automatic right for this reader to sign.</p>
 <p>The honest answer is a partner. A Dutch-speaking occupational hygienist qualifies the job, selects the model or sampling strategy, reviews interpretation and signs the professional report from the first sale. The reader manages evidence, observes the site and conducts supplementary Polish or Russian interviews. Dutch training material remains the supplier's duty under REACH; a crew-language explanation cannot replace the required expert course. <!-- CHECK: 04-reach-detail --> If the partner will not accept that division, the reader has no direct route.</p>
-<p>The precedent is Synergy Environmental Solutions in Stoke-on-Trent. Its occupational-hygiene arm markets air and biological isocyanate monitoring for vehicle refinishing, PU foam, adhesive spraying, composites and industrial coating. <!-- CHECK: 04-precedent-offer --> Companies House independently records company 07937140 as active, incorporated on 6 February 2012, with environmental consulting among its activities and accounts through March 2025. <!-- CHECK: 04-precedent-trace --> That proves the service shape can persist elsewhere. It does not transfer British rules, prices or customer behaviour to the Netherlands.</p>
+<p>The precedent is Synergy Environmental Solutions in Stoke-on-Trent. Its occupational-hygiene arm markets air and biological isocyanate monitoring for vehicle refinishing, PU foam, adhesive spraying, composites and industrial coating. <!-- CHECK: 04-precedent-offer --> Companies House independently records company 07937140 as active, incorporated on 6 February 2012, with environmental consulting among its activities and accounts through March 2025. <!-- CHECK: 04-precedent-trace --> This shows that an active, independently traceable company currently offers the service shape elsewhere. It does not prove the service's age or economics, or transfer British customer behaviour to the Netherlands.</p>
 <p>The constraint that breaks the fit is availability for real site work. Spraying cannot be reconstructed from a weekend spreadsheet, and a representative job may move at short notice. The reader needs reserved weekdays beside the day job and a partner who can attend or accept controlled fieldwork. A two-year qualification route would change the economics, but it violates the agreed retraining constraint.</p>
 </section>
 
