 <h2>The first sale</h2>
 <p>Build ten prospect types, then qualify the chemical and task rather than assuming exposure from a trade label. Screen spray-foam insulation contractors, PU-floor installers, industrial protective-coating firms, car body shops and commercial-vehicle refinishers. Add rail-coating contractors, yacht and ship painters, composite fabricators, spray-adhesive users and PU-elastomer processors. Exclude firms whose safety data sheets stay below the REACH threshold or whose work never creates the defined spray exposure.</p>
 <p>Reach them through two independent Dutch hygienists, coating and foam suppliers, training providers, industry associations and direct English or Polish notes. A supplier introduction is useful but dangerous because the supplier may own both the course and customer. The first conversation reconstructs the last product change, inspection, exposure assessment and training audit. Ask who did the work, what was measured, what was paid and whether it sat inside an arbodienst contract.</p>
-<p>The opening offer is a <strong>€1,250 design-hurdle desk triage</strong> for one process, credited into a <strong>€4,750 design-hurdle baseline</strong>. Triage checks safety data sheets, task variants, existing RI&amp;E evidence and certificates. The baseline adds the observed job, partner-reviewed quantitative assessment, action register and one Dutch management debrief. Laboratory analysis and extra measurement days are quoted after method selection and invoiced directly to the employer.</p>
+<p>The opening offer is a <strong>€1,250 design-hurdle desk triage</strong> for one process, credited into a <strong>€5,500 design-hurdle baseline</strong>. Triage checks safety data sheets, task variants, existing RI&amp;E evidence and certificates. The baseline adds the observed job, partner-reviewed quantitative assessment, action register and one Dutch management debrief. Laboratory analysis and extra measurement days are quoted after method selection and invoiced directly to the employer.</p>
 <p>The owner or operations manager signs. The order names the process, normal job date, participating crew, hygienist, access to safety data sheets and the person who owns corrective actions. Fifty percent is paid before the visit. The current limits create a reason to inspect the old file; a customer audit, process change or actual Inspectorate visit creates priority.</p>
