 <tr><td><strong>Mature design:</strong> fifty baselines and sixty change reviews across several spray trades.</td><td>50 × €5.5k plus 60 × €1.5k. <strong>Total €365k.</strong></td><td>Contract hygienist capacity €80k; field technician €65k; instruments and calibration €25k; travel and language support €15k. <strong>Gross margin €180k (49%).</strong></td><td>Founder replacement cost €100k plus €50k insurance, standards, sales and admin leaves <strong>€30k</strong> before tax and financing.</td></tr>
 </tbody></table></div>
 <p>Year one is paid evidence. Six field jobs require roughly two founder days each plus selling and coordination. It fits beside a job only with booked site days and a partner who absorbs schedule variance. The loss after founder replacement is honest: the test does not replace developer income.</p>
+<p>The mature workload assumes 35 model-only baselines, 15 measured baselines and 60 change reviews. For hygienists, allow three hours per model-only baseline, ten per measured baseline and two per review. That is 375 delivery hours, plus 25 reserve hours, at a €200 hourly hurdle: €80,000.</p>
+<p>For the technician, allow 12 hours per model-only baseline, 28 per measured baseline and five per review. That is 1,140 delivery hours plus 485 paid hours for travel, setup, idle time and training. At a €40 hourly hurdle, 1,625 paid hours cost €65,000. The 15 measured baselines consume 420 technician hours and permit work across multiple days.</p>
+<p>The founder spends five hours per baseline and three per review, or 430 delivery hours. Another 570 cover selling, partner coordination, quality control and exceptions. At a €100 replacement-cost hurdle, 1,000 founder hours produce the €100,000 line. The technician allocation is one full paid year; the founder allocation is about three fifths of that capacity.</p>
 <p>The mature model barely works. It needs one new baseline most weeks and more change reviews than baselines. There is no statutory annual renewal for the whole exposure file, so those reviews must be caused by real changes or voluntarily bought assurance. <!-- CHECK: 04-annual-boundary --> If average baseline revenue stays at the pitch's €1,500–€3,000 estimate, partner expertise and site labour consume the business.</p>
-<p>Gross margin pays professional assessment, field delivery, instruments and travel before corporate overhead. Founder replacement is owner compensation, not free labour. The €30,000 remainder is company surplus and must absorb claims, idle days and hiring variance. A mature 49% gross margin is thin for work carrying professional liability.</p>
+<p>Gross margin pays professional assessment, field delivery, instruments and travel before corporate overhead. Founder replacement is the market cost of replacing operating and sales labour. The €30,000 remainder is pre-tax company surplus, not yet distributable owner income. It still carries claims, idle-day and hiring risk. A mature 49% gross margin is thin for work carrying professional liability.</p>
 <p>Working capital stays light by billing half in advance, renting pumps, and putting laboratory and medical invoices outside the company. The <strong>year-one cash-at-risk design hurdle is €12,000</strong> for insurance advice, partner deposits, training, travel and rentals. Spend no more than €4,500 before first payment. Do not buy a van, pump fleet or training platform. That keeps the experiment far below the €50,000 year-one ceiling.</p>
 </section>
 
